.\" Manual page for ncpatcher.
.TH NCPATCHER 1 "2026" "ncpatcher" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ncpatcher \- compile code and splice it into a Nintendo DS ROM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncpatcher
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ncpatcher
compiles C, C++ and assembly with a cross-toolchain and patches the result into
a Nintendo DS ROM's ARM binaries and overlays. What it builds, and where it
writes it, is described by
.B ncpatcher.yaml
in the project directory.
.PP
With no command it builds, which is how existing projects and the level editor
invoke it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Compile and patch. The default.
.TP
.BR clean " [" \-\-backups ]
Delete the build directories. With
.BR \-\-backups ,
also delete the backup directory \(em which leaves the ROM binaries patched with
no way back, so
.B restore
is usually what was meant.
.TP
.B restore
Copy the pristine binaries out of the backup directory back into the ROM
directory, then remove the backups.
.TP
.BR "config dump" " [" \-\-explain ] " [" \-\-json ]
Print every setting after inheritance, variables and globs have been resolved:
what the build would actually use, not what the file says.
.B \-\-explain
adds where each setting came from.
.TP
.B config validate
Load and resolve the configuration, reporting problems, without building.
.TP
.B config path
Print the path of the configuration file that would be used.
.TP
.BR migrate " [" \-\-write ]
Convert a version 1
.B ncpatcher.json
into a commented
.BR ncpatcher.yaml ,
hoisting shared flags and extracting
.B \-D
flags into a
.B defines
list. Prints the result;
.B \-\-write
saves it.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " PATH" "\fR, \fP" \-\-project " PATH"
Project directory, or the configuration file itself. Removes the need to launch
the program from the project directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-rom " PATH"
Extracted-ROM directory, overriding the one in the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-D " NAME[=VAL]" "\fR, \fP" \-\-define " NAME[=VAL]"
Define a preprocessor macro for every translation unit.
.TP
.BI \-\-var " NAME=VAL"
Set a configuration variable, overriding
.B vars:
in the project file. Lets one committed configuration serve a machine whose
reference tree lives somewhere unusual.
.TP
.BI \-\-toolchain " PREFIX"
Cross-compiler prefix, for example
.BR arm-none-eabi- .
.TP
.BI \-j " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-jobs " N"
Compile jobs to run at once. 0 uses one per hardware thread.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable every category of verbose output.
.TP
.BI \-\-verbose-tag " TAG"
Enable one category: build, section, elf, patch, library, linking, symbols,
nolib, all.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
When to style the console output.
.B NO_COLOR
in the environment is honoured.
.TP
.BI \-\-message-format " human|json"
.B json
emits one JSON object per line on stdout and moves the human log to stderr, so
that a caller has exactly one thing to parse.
.TP
.BI \-\-result " PATH"
Write a JSON summary of the run \(em status, counts, diagnostics and the
artifacts written \(em to this file.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " PATH"
Write the log file here instead of the default
.IR <buildDir>/ncpatcher.log .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-log
Do not write a log file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Internal error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong.
.TP
.B 3
The configuration could not be loaded or resolved.
.TP
.B 4
A module could not be resolved.
.TP
.B 5
The toolchain is missing or unusable.
.TP
.B 6
Compilation failed.
.TP
.B 7
Linking failed.
.TP
.B 8
Patching failed.
.TP
.B 9
The ROM could not be read or written.
.TP
.B 10
A pre-build or post-build command failed.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCPATCHER_TOOLCHAIN
Cross-compiler prefix, used when the command line does not say.
.TP
.B NCPATCHER_JOBS
Compile jobs, used when the command line does not say.
.TP
.B NCPATCHER_LOG
Log file path, used when the command line does not say.
.TP
.B NCPATCHER_DATA_DIR
Directory holding
.BR ncp.h ", " ncp_ide.h " and " ncprt.c .
Searched before the install location, for development trees and images that
place them somewhere of their own choosing.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, the console output is not styled.
.PP
Precedence throughout is command line, then environment, then the project file,
then the built-in default.
.B ncpatcher config dump \-\-explain
says which of them won.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ncpatcher.yaml
The project configuration. An
.I ncpatcher.json
is read as the older version 1 schema, which stays supported.
.TP
.I <buildDir>/ncpatcher.log
The log of the last build.
.TP
.I <dataDir>/ncp.h
Force-included into every translation unit. Looked for in
.BR $NCPATCHER_DATA_DIR ,
then
.I <exeDir>/../share/ncpatcher
, then next to the executable.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README, installed alongside this page, documents the configuration
schema in full.
